The graph of $y = \tan x$ is shown below on the domain $[-\pi, \pi]$.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[every node/.style={font=\large}]
\begin{axis}[axis lines=middle, xlabel={$x$}, ylabel={$y$},
  xmin=-3.6, xmax=3.6, ymin=-4, ymax=4,
  xtick={-3.1416, -1.5708, 1.5708, 3.1416},
  xticklabels={$-\pi$, $-\frac{\pi}{2}$, $\frac{\pi}{2}$, $\pi$},
  ytick={-3, -2, -1, 1, 2, 3},
  samples=200, clip=false,
  restrict y to domain=-4:4, unbounded coords=jump,
  axis line style={-{Stealth}}, width=11cm, height=6.5cm]
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=-3.13:-1.69] {tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=-1.45:1.45] {tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[smooth, thick, blue, domain=1.69:3.13] {tan(deg(x))};
\addplot[dashed, gray, domain=-4:4] ({-1.5708},{x});
\addplot[dashed, gray, domain=-4:4] ({1.5708},{x});
\end{axis}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What are the equations of the vertical asymptotes of $y = \tan x$ in the domain $[-\pi, \pi]$?
